mod backend.compiler.names;

/**
 * NAME RESOLUTION: what a name in a body means
 *
 *      total = count * price;      three names. Each is a local variable, a parameter, a field of
 *                                  the class or of a class above it, a global of the module or of
 *                                  an imported module, a class, an enum value ... or a mistake.
 *
 * This package ANSWERS the question and builds no tree: it returns a
 * `lookup_result` and the expression code (backend/compiler/expressions)
 * decides what to make of it. It is the bootstrap's version of the C++
 * compiler's dependency/dependency.cpp, in pieces.
 *
 * The files of this package (module `backend.compiler.names`):
 *
 *      names.sharp             this front door
 *      lookup_result.sharp     what a name was found to be
 *      name_lookup.sharp       a plain name: locals, the class and its bases, the modules the file sees
 *      class_members.sharp     the member of a class called so-and-so, through the base chain
 *      access_rules.sharp      private / protected / local; instance members from static code
 *      not_found.sharp         "there is no ..." for a plain name: did-you-mean, and "it exists, but ..."
 *      other_language_habits.sharp  ... when the unknown name is another language's way of writing
 *                              something: `total = 0;`, `f(width = 2)`, `for(i; ...)`, `brake;`
 *      no_member.sharp         "... has no member named ..." for `point.z` and `std.io#prnt`
 *      visible_names.sharp     every name visible from a place, for did-you-mean
 *
 * This file is the package's front door: it only says what is where.
 */
